          "collection_date": "2001",
          "description": {
            "comment": "Annotated genome assembly of Aphis gossypii from the Pest Genomics Initiative. Multi-individual but clonal so only 2 haplotypes observed when snp/indel calling so potentially equivalent to single individual data. Resulting Falcon assembly were separated to two species using Aphis gossypii Illumina mapping. Haplotig removal and manual curation. Hi-C used to scaffold to chromosome level. Maker annotation pipeline used with both transcriptome transfer and de novo gene prediction as inputs to Evigene to pick best gene models. Curation of P450, ABC, UGT, IRAC gene models where RNA-seq evidence was present. Multi-individual taken for CLR PacBio (contaminated with myzus persicae) and multi-individual for Hi-C and 10X illumina sequencing. Bayer culture since 2001, collected from cucumber greehouse in Hohenheim Germany.",
